          "label": "points into"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reads must mirror writes in order",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 64,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "red",
          "at": 5000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Special objects are flat_binder_object structs: a type tag plus a binder pointer or handle.",
      "narration": "Each special object is a flat_binder_object. A type tag says whether it is a local binder, a remote handle or a file descriptor.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "flat_binder_object",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "c",
          "text": "struct flat_binder_object {\n  struct binder_object_header hdr;\n  __u32 flags;\n  union {\n    binder_uintptr_t binder;\n    __u32 handle;\n  };\n  binder_uintptr_t cookie;\n};",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 36,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 4000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "The driver rewrites each object for the receiver: binder becomes handle, fd becomes a new fd.",
      "narration": "The driver walks the offsets and rewrites each object. A local binder becomes a handle in the receiver, and a file descriptor is duplicated into its fd table.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Driver translation",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "BINDER_TYPE_BINDER -> HANDLE",
            "BINDER_TYPE_HANDLE -> HANDLE or BINDER",
            "BINDER_TYPE_FD -> new fd in receiver"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "purple",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Owner process gets its own local pointer back",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 50,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "color": "gray",
          "at": 5500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "caption": "Only the offsets are parsed in the kernel; the rest of the payload stays opaque bytes.",
      "narration": "That is why offsets exist. The kernel parses just the marked objects and never interprets the rest of the data.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Why offsets",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "k",
